WHAT WAS TAKEN. Two font files, whole:
`public/fonts/jetbrains-mono-latin.woff2` and
`public/fonts/jetbrains-mono-latin-ext.woff2`.

This project sets every numeric readout in it — coordinates, altitudes, MGRS,
counts — because the cockpit puts figures in columns that must not shuffle when
a 1 becomes a 7 (`--font-mono` in `style.css`).

Until 2026-09-09 the face was loaded over a `<link>` to Google Fonts and no
file was ours to redistribute. The link was removed for two reasons, both
recorded in `index.html`: it blocked the first paint on an origin the browser
had never resolved, and it sent every visitor's IP to `fonts.gstatic.com`
before they had consented to anything (CJUE, 2022).

WHAT WAS CHANGED. Nothing. These are Google's own woff2 builds, byte for byte
as served; only the `src:` URL in the stylesheet points here instead of there.
The variable weight axis (300-700) and the unicode-range split are Google's
subsetting, not ours.

OFL 1.1 permits this redistribution as part of a larger work. The reserved-font
-name clause (§5) is not engaged: the font is unmodified and served under its
own name.
